[[Open This|Rate Limits is a Thing]]

---

When you get something like this:

```
Rate limit exceeded; see https://docs.gitlab.com/user/gitlab_com/rate_limits/ for more details
```

https://docs.gitlab.com/user/gitlab_com/rate_limits/

```bash
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://gitlab.com/users/sign_in
```

* `200` means you’re unblocked.
* `429` means you’re still rate-limited. Wait a bit longer.
* `403` means GitLab blocked the IP for a longer period. If that’s still showing in an hour, contact GitLab Support with your public IP, which you can get with `curl -s ifconfig.me`.

To avoid this in the future, don’t leave job or pipeline pages open in tabs. They keep checking the server for new log output for as long as they’re open.
